curtsy (0.3.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Cut data-plane syscall overhead across the TCP/UDP relays:
    - TCP: cached timer deadlines with throttled sweeps, 1024-event epoll
      batches, batched budget release, connection freelist, and one less
      epoll_ctl per closed connection.
    - UDP: 50ms-throttled expiry sweeps, idle-time-scheduled sockmap
      session checks (99% fewer bpf() calls under steer-heavy load),
      per-wake timestamp reuse, pointer-based association access, faster
      SocketAddr hashing, pre-sized session maps, rate-limited drop logs,
      and a cooldown after sockmap pairing failures.
    - Logging now emits one write syscall per line; the tuning daemon
      loads its kprobe observer only when a limit is auto-tuned.
  * Add performance.udpDatagramBufferBytes to size the batched UDP
    receive slots (576..65536, default 65536).
  * Build for the architecture baseline CPU by default; pass
    -Dcpu=native for host-optimized binaries.

 -- Curtsy contributors <maintainers@example.invalid>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

